IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `uc-core`
IMPORT `uc2-part6-ch2-self-employed`

-- The Universal Credit Regulations 2013 (S.I. 2013/376), Part 6, Chapter 4 (MISCELLANEOUS): regulations 75 to 77.
-- Source: ../../registers/source-bundle/uksi-2013-376.txt (lines 1204-1264), a plain-text rendering made by a converter script; it is not the official text.
-- Target: the stable build 1.6.98. Money is a NUMBER of pounds; a calculated amount is rounded once, at the end, with the keel's
-- `core — an amount rounded to the nearest penny` (regulation 6(1)).
--
-- Regulations 75 and 76 decide what is NOT counted: a sum, a payment or an income is "disregarded" in the calculation of capital or
-- of unearned income. Each rule below answers whether the thing the paragraph names is disregarded; the caller asks it of the item
-- that paragraph names (the sum, the regular payments, the annuity payments, the trust capital or income). Regulation 77 imports
-- the self-employed earnings module because it sends the company's income through regulation 57.

§ `Part 6, Chapter 4 -- Miscellaneous`

§§ `Chapter heading`
-- src:1204 | CHAPTER 4 — MISCELLANEOUS

§§ `Regulation 75 -- Compensation for personal injury`

-- src:1205 | 75 Compensation for personal injury
-- src:1206 | (1) This regulation applies where a sum has been awarded to a person, or has been agreed by or behalf of a person, in consequence of a personal injury to that person.
-- src:1207 | (2) If, in accordance with an order of the court or an agreement, the person receives all or part of that sum by way of regular payments, those payments are to be disregarded in the calculation of the person's unearned income.
-- src:1208 | (3) If the sum has been used to purchase an annuity, payments under the annuity are to be disregarded in the calculation of the person's unearned income.
-- src:1209 | (4) If the sum is held in trust, any capital of the trust derived from that sum is to be disregarded in the calculation of the person's capital and any income from the trust is to be disregarded in the calculation of the person's unearned income.
-- src:1210 | (5) If the sum is administered by the court on behalf of the person or can only be disposed of by direction of the court, it is to be disregarded in the calculation of the person's capital and any regular payments from that amount are to be disregarded in the calculation of the person's unearned income.
-- src:1211 | (6) If the sum is not held in trust or has not been used to purchase an annuity or otherwise disposed of, but has been paid to the person within the past 12 months, that sum is to be disregarded in the calculation of the person's capital.
@ref reg 75 (src:1205-1211)
DECLARE `Sum awarded in consequence of a personal injury` HAS
    `sum awarded to the person, or agreed by or on behalf of the person, in consequence of a personal injury to that person`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `in accordance with an order of the court or an agreement, the person receives all or part of the sum by way of regular payments`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the sum has been used to purchase an annuity`                                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `the sum is held in trust`                                                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the sum is administered by the court on behalf of the person or can only be disposed of by direction of the court`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the sum has otherwise been disposed of`                                                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `date on which the sum was paid to the person`                                              IS A MAYBE DATE

-- Paragraph (1): the regulation applies where a sum has been awarded, or agreed by or on behalf of the person, in consequence of a
-- personal injury to that person.
-- src:1206 | (1) This regulation applies where a sum has been awarded to a person, or has been agreed by or behalf of a person, in consequence of a personal injury to that person.
@ref reg 75(1) (src:1206)
GIVEN sum IS A `Sum awarded in consequence of a personal injury`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 75(1) — this regulation applies to the sum` sum MEANS
    sum's `sum awarded to the person, or agreed by or on behalf of the person, in consequence of a personal injury to that person`

-- Paragraph (2): regular payments of all or part of the sum are disregarded in the calculation of unearned income.
-- src:1207 | (2) If, in accordance with an order of the court or an agreement, the person receives all or part of that sum by way of regular payments, those payments are to be disregarded in the calculation of the person's unearned income.
@ref reg 75(2) (src:1207)
GIVEN sum IS A `Sum awarded in consequence of a personal injury`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 75(2) — the regular payments are disregarded in the calculation of unearned income` sum MEANS
        (`reg 75(1) — this regulation applies to the sum` sum)
    AND (sum's `in accordance with an order of the court or an agreement, the person receives all or part of the sum by way of regular payments`)

-- Paragraph (3): payments under an annuity bought with the sum are disregarded in the calculation of unearned income.
-- src:1208 | (3) If the sum has been used to purchase an annuity, payments under the annuity are to be disregarded in the calculation of the person's unearned income.
@ref reg 75(3) (src:1208)
GIVEN sum IS A `Sum awarded in consequence of a personal injury`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 75(3) — the annuity payments are disregarded in the calculation of unearned income` sum MEANS
        (`reg 75(1) — this regulation applies to the sum` sum)
    AND (sum's `the sum has been used to purchase an annuity`)

-- Paragraph (4): where the sum is held in trust, any capital of the trust derived from it is disregarded in the calculation of
-- capital and any income from the trust is disregarded in the calculation of unearned income. Both are disregarded under the same
-- condition, so the one rule answers either question.
-- src:1209 | (4) If the sum is held in trust, any capital of the trust derived from that sum is to be disregarded in the calculation of the person's capital and any income from the trust is to be disregarded in the calculation of the person's unearned income.
@ref reg 75(4) (src:1209)
GIVEN sum IS A `Sum awarded in consequence of a personal injury`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 75(4) — the capital of the trust or the income from it is disregarded` sum MEANS
        (`reg 75(1) — this regulation applies to the sum` sum)
    AND (sum's `the sum is held in trust`)

-- Paragraph (5): where the sum is administered by the court on behalf of the person, or can only be disposed of by direction of the
-- court, it is disregarded in the calculation of capital and any regular payments from it are disregarded in the calculation of
-- unearned income. Both under the same condition.
-- src:1210 | (5) If the sum is administered by the court on behalf of the person or can only be disposed of by direction of the court, it is to be disregarded in the calculation of the person's capital and any regular payments from that amount are to be disregarded in the calculation of the person's unearned income.
@ref reg 75(5) (src:1210)
GIVEN sum IS A `Sum awarded in consequence of a personal injury`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 75(5) — the sum or the regular payments from it are disregarded` sum MEANS
        (`reg 75(1) — this regulation applies to the sum` sum)
    AND (sum's `the sum is administered by the court on behalf of the person or can only be disposed of by direction of the court`)

-- Paragraph (6): a sum that is not held in trust, has not been used to buy an annuity or otherwise been disposed of, but was paid to
-- the person within the past 12 months, is disregarded in the calculation of capital. The 12 months run back from the date on which
-- the capital is calculated, the last day counting (fork F-M1).
-- src:1211 | (6) If the sum is not held in trust or has not been used to purchase an annuity or otherwise disposed of, but has been paid to the person within the past 12 months, that sum is to be disregarded in the calculation of the person's capital.
@ref reg 75(6) (src:1211)
GIVEN sum IS A `Sum awarded in consequence of a personal injury`
      `calculated on` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 75(6) — the sum is disregarded in the calculation of capital` sum `calculated on` MEANS
        (`reg 75(1) — this regulation applies to the sum` sum)
    AND (NOT (sum's `the sum is held in trust`))
    AND (NOT (sum's `the sum has been used to purchase an annuity`))
    AND (NOT (sum's `the sum has otherwise been disposed of`))
    AND (CONSIDER sum's `date on which the sum was paid to the person`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
         WHEN JUST paid THEN (paid AT MOST `calculated on`) AND (`calculated on` AT MOST (`core — the date reached by adding a time limit to a date` paid (`Time limit` WITH quantity IS 12, unit IS months))))

§§ `Regulation 76 -- Special schemes for compensation etc.`

-- Paragraph (1): a payment from a scheme established or approved by the Secretary of State, or from a trust established with funds
-- provided by the Secretary of State, for the purpose of (a) compensation or support in respect of one of the listed events or
-- conditions, or (b) supporting persons with a disability to live independently in their accommodation. Sub-paragraph (a)(vi) and
-- the words after (a)(iii) and (a)(v) are runs of dots or full stops in this text.
-- src:1212 | 76 Special schemes for compensation etc.
-- src:1213 | (1) This regulation applies where a person receives a payment from a scheme established or approved by the Secretary of State or from a trust established with funds provided by the Secretary of State for the purpose of—
-- src:1214 | (a) providing compensation or support in respect of any of the following—
-- src:1215 | (i) a person having been diagnosed with variant Creutzfeldt-Jacob disease or infected from contaminated blood products,
-- src:1216 | (ii) the bombings in London on 7th July 2005,
-- src:1217 | (iii) persons who have been interned or suffered forced labour, injury, property loss or loss of a child during the Second World War; ...
-- src:1218 | (iv) the terrorist attacks in London on 22nd March 2017 or 3rd June 2017,
-- src:1219 | (v) the bombing in Manchester on 22nd May 2017; ...
-- src:1220 | (vi) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
-- src:1221 | (vii) historic institutional child abuse in the United Kingdom;
-- src:1222 | (b) supporting persons with a disability to live independently in their accommodation.
-- src:1223 | (1A) This regulation also applies where a person receives a payment from—
-- src:1224 | (a) the National Emergencies Trust, registered charity number 1182809;
-- src:1225 | (b) the Child Migrants Trust, registered charity number 1171479, under the scheme for former British child migrants; ...
-- src:1226 | (c) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
-- src:1227 | (d) the scheme established by the Windrush Compensation Scheme (Expenditure) Act 2020...
-- src:1228 | (e) the Post Office or the Secretary of State for the purpose of providing compensation or support which is—
-- src:1229 | (i) in connection with the failings of the Horizon system; or
-- src:1230 | (ii) otherwise payable following the judgment in Bates and Others v Post Office Ltd ((No. 3) “Common Issues”); ...
-- src:1231 | (f) the Victims of Overseas Terrorism Compensation Scheme established by the Ministry of Justice in 2012 under section 47 of the Crime and Security Act 2010; or
-- src:1232 | (g) the Lesbian, Gay, Bisexual and Transgender Financial Recognition Scheme administered under the authority of the Secretary of State for Defence.
-- src:1233 | (1B) This regulation also applies where a person receives a payment made for the purpose of providing compensation or support in respect of the fire on 14th June 2017 at Grenfell Tower.
-- src:1234 | (1C) This regulation also applies where a person—
-- src:1235 | (a) receives a vaccine damage payment or is a person for whose benefit a vaccine damage payment is made;
-- src:1236 | (b) is the partner of a person referred to in sub-paragraph (a) and receives a payment by or on behalf of that person which is derived from a vaccine damage payment;
-- src:1237 | (c) was the partner of a person referred to in sub-paragraph (a) immediately before the latter’s death and receives a payment from their estate which is derived from a vaccine damage payment;
-- src:1238 | (d) in a case where a vaccine damage payment is made to the personal representative of a person who was severely disabled as a result of vaccination (“P”), was P’s partner immediately before P’s death and receives a payment from P’s estate which is derived from a vaccine damage payment.
-- src:1239 | (1D) This regulation also applies where a person—
-- src:1240 | (a) receives a miscarriage of justice compensation payment or is a person for whose benefit such a payment is made;
-- src:1241 | (b) is the partner of a person to whom sub-paragraph (a) refers, and receives a payment by or on behalf of that person which is derived from the miscarriage of justice compensation payment;
-- src:1242 | (c) was the partner of a person to whom sub-paragraph (a) refers immediately before their death and receives a payment from their estate which is derived from a miscarriage of justice compensation payment;
-- src:1243 | (d) in a case where a miscarriage of justice compensation payment is made to the personal representative of a deceased person (“P”), was P’s partner immediately before P’s death and receives a payment from P’s estate which is derived from the miscarriage of justice compensation payment.
-- src:1244 | (2) Any such payment, if it is capital, is to be disregarded in the calculation of the person's capital and, if it is income, is to be disregarded in the calculation of the person's income.
-- src:1245 | (3) In relation to a claim for universal credit made by a person other than the diagnosed or infected person referred to in paragraph (1)(a)(i), a payment received from the scheme or trust or which derives from a payment received from the scheme or trust, is to be disregarded if it would be disregarded in relation to an award of state pension credit by virtue of paragraph 13 or 15 of Schedule 5 to the State Pension Credit Regulations 2002.
@ref reg 76 (src:1212-1245)
DECLARE `Payment considered under regulation 76` HAS
    `payment from a scheme established or approved by the Secretary of State, or from a trust established with funds provided by the Secretary of State`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `purpose: compensation or support for a person diagnosed with variant Creutzfeldt-Jacob disease or infected from contaminated blood products`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `purpose: compensation or support in respect of the bombings in London on 7th July 2005`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `purpose: compensation or support for persons who have been interned or suffered forced labour, injury, property loss or loss of a child during the Second World War`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `purpose: compensation or support in respect of the terrorist attacks in London on 22nd March 2017 or 3rd June 2017`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `purpose: compensation or support in respect of the bombing in Manchester on 22nd May 2017`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `purpose: compensation or support in respect of historic institutional child abuse in the United Kingdom`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `purpose: supporting persons with a disability to live independently in their accommodation`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `payment from the National Emergencies Trust, registered charity number 1182809`           IS A BOOLEAN
    `payment from the Child Migrants Trust, registered charity number 1171479, under the scheme for former British child migrants`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `payment from the scheme established by the Windrush Compensation Scheme (Expenditure) Act 2020`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `payment from the Post Office or the Secretary of State for the purpose of providing compensation or support in connection with the failings of the Horizon system`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `payment from the Post Office or the Secretary of State for the purpose of providing compensation or support otherwise payable following the judgment in Bates and Others v Post Office Ltd (No. 3) (Common Issues)`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `payment from the Victims of Overseas Terrorism Compensation Scheme established by the Ministry of Justice in 2012 under section 47 of the Crime and Security Act 2010`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `payment from the Lesbian, Gay, Bisexual and Transgender Financial Recognition Scheme administered under the authority of the Secretary of State for Defence`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `payment made for the purpose of providing compensation or support in respect of the fire on 14th June 2017 at Grenfell Tower`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person receives a vaccine damage payment or is a person for whose benefit a vaccine damage payment is made`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is the partner of a person referred to in regulation 76(1C)(a) and receives a payment by or on behalf of that person which is derived from a vaccine damage payment`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person was the partner of a person referred to in regulation 76(1C)(a) immediately before the latter's death and receives a payment from their estate which is derived from a vaccine damage payment`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `a vaccine damage payment is made to the personal representative of a person who was severely disabled as a result of vaccination (P), and the person was P's partner immediately before P's death and receives a payment from P's estate which is derived from a vaccine damage payment`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person receives a miscarriage of justice compensation payment or is a person for whose benefit such a payment is made`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is the partner of a person referred to in regulation 76(1D)(a) and receives a payment by or on behalf of that person which is derived from the miscarriage of justice compensation payment`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person was the partner of a person referred to in regulation 76(1D)(a) immediately before their death and receives a payment from their estate which is derived from a miscarriage of justice compensation payment`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `a miscarriage of justice compensation payment is made to the personal representative of a deceased person (P), and the person was P's partner immediately before P's death and receives a payment from P's estate which is derived from the miscarriage of justice compensation payment`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the payment is capital`                                                                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `the claim is made by a person other than the diagnosed or infected person referred to in regulation 76(1)(a)(i)`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the payment is received from the scheme or trust, or derives from a payment received from it, and would be disregarded in relation to an award of state pension credit by virtue of paragraph 13 or 15 of Schedule 5 to the State Pension Credit Regulations 2002`  IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:1213 | (1) This regulation applies where a person receives a payment from a scheme established or approved by the Secretary of State or from a trust established with funds provided by the Secretary of State for the purpose of—
-- src:1214 | (a) providing compensation or support in respect of any of the following—
-- src:1215 | (i) a person having been diagnosed with variant Creutzfeldt-Jacob disease or infected from contaminated blood products,
-- src:1216 | (ii) the bombings in London on 7th July 2005,
-- src:1217 | (iii) persons who have been interned or suffered forced labour, injury, property loss or loss of a child during the Second World War; ...
-- src:1218 | (iv) the terrorist attacks in London on 22nd March 2017 or 3rd June 2017,
-- src:1219 | (v) the bombing in Manchester on 22nd May 2017; ...
-- src:1220 | (vi) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
-- src:1221 | (vii) historic institutional child abuse in the United Kingdom;
-- src:1222 | (b) supporting persons with a disability to live independently in their accommodation.
@ref reg 76(1) (src:1213-1222)
GIVEN payment IS A `Payment considered under regulation 76`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 76(1)(a) — the purpose is compensation or support for one of the listed events or conditions` payment MEANS
        (payment's `purpose: compensation or support for a person diagnosed with variant Creutzfeldt-Jacob disease or infected from contaminated blood products`)
    OR  (payment's `purpose: compensation or support in respect of the bombings in London on 7th July 2005`)
    OR  (payment's `purpose: compensation or support for persons who have been interned or suffered forced labour, injury, property loss or loss of a child during the Second World War`)
    OR  (payment's `purpose: compensation or support in respect of the terrorist attacks in London on 22nd March 2017 or 3rd June 2017`)
    OR  (payment's `purpose: compensation or support in respect of the bombing in Manchester on 22nd May 2017`)
    OR  (payment's `purpose: compensation or support in respect of historic institutional child abuse in the United Kingdom`)

-- src:1213 | (1) This regulation applies where a person receives a payment from a scheme established or approved by the Secretary of State or from a trust established with funds provided by the Secretary of State for the purpose of—
-- src:1214 | (a) providing compensation or support in respect of any of the following—
-- src:1215 | (i) a person having been diagnosed with variant Creutzfeldt-Jacob disease or infected from contaminated blood products,
-- src:1216 | (ii) the bombings in London on 7th July 2005,
-- src:1217 | (iii) persons who have been interned or suffered forced labour, injury, property loss or loss of a child during the Second World War; ...
-- src:1218 | (iv) the terrorist attacks in London on 22nd March 2017 or 3rd June 2017,
-- src:1219 | (v) the bombing in Manchester on 22nd May 2017; ...
-- src:1220 | (vi) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
-- src:1221 | (vii) historic institutional child abuse in the United Kingdom;
-- src:1222 | (b) supporting persons with a disability to live independently in their accommodation.
@ref reg 76(1) (src:1213-1222)
GIVEN payment IS A `Payment considered under regulation 76`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 76(1) — the payment is from a scheme or trust of the Secretary of State for a listed purpose` payment MEANS
        (payment's `payment from a scheme established or approved by the Secretary of State, or from a trust established with funds provided by the Secretary of State`)
    AND (    (`reg 76(1)(a) — the purpose is compensation or support for one of the listed events or conditions` payment)
          OR (payment's `purpose: supporting persons with a disability to live independently in their accommodation`))

-- src:1223 | (1A) This regulation also applies where a person receives a payment from—
-- src:1224 | (a) the National Emergencies Trust, registered charity number 1182809;
-- src:1225 | (b) the Child Migrants Trust, registered charity number 1171479, under the scheme for former British child migrants; ...
-- src:1226 | (c) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
-- src:1227 | (d) the scheme established by the Windrush Compensation Scheme (Expenditure) Act 2020...
-- src:1228 | (e) the Post Office or the Secretary of State for the purpose of providing compensation or support which is—
-- src:1229 | (i) in connection with the failings of the Horizon system; or
-- src:1230 | (ii) otherwise payable following the judgment in Bates and Others v Post Office Ltd ((No. 3) “Common Issues”); ...
-- src:1231 | (f) the Victims of Overseas Terrorism Compensation Scheme established by the Ministry of Justice in 2012 under section 47 of the Crime and Security Act 2010; or
-- src:1232 | (g) the Lesbian, Gay, Bisexual and Transgender Financial Recognition Scheme administered under the authority of the Secretary of State for Defence.
@ref reg 76(1A) (src:1223-1232)
GIVEN payment IS A `Payment considered under regulation 76`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 76(1A) — the payment is from one of the listed bodies or schemes` payment MEANS
        (payment's `payment from the National Emergencies Trust, registered charity number 1182809`)
    OR  (payment's `payment from the Child Migrants Trust, registered charity number 1171479, under the scheme for former British child migrants`)
    OR  (payment's `payment from the scheme established by the Windrush Compensation Scheme (Expenditure) Act 2020`)
    OR  (payment's `payment from the Post Office or the Secretary of State for the purpose of providing compensation or support in connection with the failings of the Horizon system`)
    OR  (payment's `payment from the Post Office or the Secretary of State for the purpose of providing compensation or support otherwise payable following the judgment in Bates and Others v Post Office Ltd (No. 3) (Common Issues)`)
    OR  (payment's `payment from the Victims of Overseas Terrorism Compensation Scheme established by the Ministry of Justice in 2012 under section 47 of the Crime and Security Act 2010`)
    OR  (payment's `payment from the Lesbian, Gay, Bisexual and Transgender Financial Recognition Scheme administered under the authority of the Secretary of State for Defence`)

-- src:1233 | (1B) This regulation also applies where a person receives a payment made for the purpose of providing compensation or support in respect of the fire on 14th June 2017 at Grenfell Tower.
@ref reg 76(1B) (src:1233)
GIVEN payment IS A `Payment considered under regulation 76`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 76(1B) — the payment is for the Grenfell Tower fire` payment MEANS
    payment's `payment made for the purpose of providing compensation or support in respect of the fire on 14th June 2017 at Grenfell Tower`

-- src:1234 | (1C) This regulation also applies where a person—
-- src:1235 | (a) receives a vaccine damage payment or is a person for whose benefit a vaccine damage payment is made;
-- src:1236 | (b) is the partner of a person referred to in sub-paragraph (a) and receives a payment by or on behalf of that person which is derived from a vaccine damage payment;
-- src:1237 | (c) was the partner of a person referred to in sub-paragraph (a) immediately before the latter’s death and receives a payment from their estate which is derived from a vaccine damage payment;
-- src:1238 | (d) in a case where a vaccine damage payment is made to the personal representative of a person who was severely disabled as a result of vaccination (“P”), was P’s partner immediately before P’s death and receives a payment from P’s estate which is derived from a vaccine damage payment.
@ref reg 76(1C) (src:1234-1238)
GIVEN payment IS A `Payment considered under regulation 76`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 76(1C) — the payment is a vaccine damage payment or derives from one` payment MEANS
        (payment's `the person receives a vaccine damage payment or is a person for whose benefit a vaccine damage payment is made`)
    OR  (payment's `the person is the partner of a person referred to in regulation 76(1C)(a) and receives a payment by or on behalf of that person which is derived from a vaccine damage payment`)
    OR  (payment's `the person was the partner of a person referred to in regulation 76(1C)(a) immediately before the latter's death and receives a payment from their estate which is derived from a vaccine damage payment`)
    OR  (payment's `a vaccine damage payment is made to the personal representative of a person who was severely disabled as a result of vaccination (P), and the person was P's partner immediately before P's death and receives a payment from P's estate which is derived from a vaccine damage payment`)

-- src:1239 | (1D) This regulation also applies where a person—
-- src:1240 | (a) receives a miscarriage of justice compensation payment or is a person for whose benefit such a payment is made;
-- src:1241 | (b) is the partner of a person to whom sub-paragraph (a) refers, and receives a payment by or on behalf of that person which is derived from the miscarriage of justice compensation payment;
-- src:1242 | (c) was the partner of a person to whom sub-paragraph (a) refers immediately before their death and receives a payment from their estate which is derived from a miscarriage of justice compensation payment;
-- src:1243 | (d) in a case where a miscarriage of justice compensation payment is made to the personal representative of a deceased person (“P”), was P’s partner immediately before P’s death and receives a payment from P’s estate which is derived from the miscarriage of justice compensation payment.
@ref reg 76(1D) (src:1239-1243)
GIVEN payment IS A `Payment considered under regulation 76`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 76(1D) — the payment is a miscarriage of justice compensation payment or derives from one` payment MEANS
        (payment's `the person receives a miscarriage of justice compensation payment or is a person for whose benefit such a payment is made`)
    OR  (payment's `the person is the partner of a person referred to in regulation 76(1D)(a) and receives a payment by or on behalf of that person which is derived from the miscarriage of justice compensation payment`)
    OR  (payment's `the person was the partner of a person referred to in regulation 76(1D)(a) immediately before their death and receives a payment from their estate which is derived from a miscarriage of justice compensation payment`)
    OR  (payment's `a miscarriage of justice compensation payment is made to the personal representative of a deceased person (P), and the person was P's partner immediately before P's death and receives a payment from P's estate which is derived from the miscarriage of justice compensation payment`)

-- Paragraph (2): a payment to which the regulation applies is disregarded in the calculation of capital if it is capital and in the
-- calculation of income if it is income; it is disregarded either way, so the rule says only that it is disregarded.
-- src:1244 | (2) Any such payment, if it is capital, is to be disregarded in the calculation of the person's capital and, if it is income, is to be disregarded in the calculation of the person's income.
@ref reg 76(2) (src:1244)
GIVEN payment IS A `Payment considered under regulation 76`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 76(2) — the payment is disregarded` payment MEANS
        (`reg 76(1) — the payment is from a scheme or trust of the Secretary of State for a listed purpose` payment)
    OR  (`reg 76(1A) — the payment is from one of the listed bodies or schemes` payment)
    OR  (`reg 76(1B) — the payment is for the Grenfell Tower fire` payment)
    OR  (`reg 76(1C) — the payment is a vaccine damage payment or derives from one` payment)
    OR  (`reg 76(1D) — the payment is a miscarriage of justice compensation payment or derives from one` payment)

-- Paragraph (3): in relation to a claim for universal credit by a person other than the diagnosed or infected person of (1)(a)(i), a
-- payment received from the scheme or trust, or which derives from one received from it, is disregarded if it would be disregarded in
-- relation to state pension credit by virtue of paragraph 13 or 15 of Schedule 5 to the State Pension Credit Regulations 2002 (a
-- stated fact: that Schedule is not an input).
-- src:1245 | (3) In relation to a claim for universal credit made by a person other than the diagnosed or infected person referred to in paragraph (1)(a)(i), a payment received from the scheme or trust or which derives from a payment received from the scheme or trust, is to be disregarded if it would be disregarded in relation to an award of state pension credit by virtue of paragraph 13 or 15 of Schedule 5 to the State Pension Credit Regulations 2002.
@ref reg 76(3) (src:1245)
GIVEN payment IS A `Payment considered under regulation 76`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 76(3) — the payment is disregarded for a claim by another person` payment MEANS
        (payment's `the claim is made by a person other than the diagnosed or infected person referred to in regulation 76(1)(a)(i)`)
    AND (payment's `the payment is received from the scheme or trust, or derives from a payment received from it, and would be disregarded in relation to an award of state pension credit by virtue of paragraph 13 or 15 of Schedule 5 to the State Pension Credit Regulations 2002`)

-- The payment is disregarded under (2) or (3).
-- src:1244 | (2) Any such payment, if it is capital, is to be disregarded in the calculation of the person's capital and, if it is income, is to be disregarded in the calculation of the person's income.
-- src:1245 | (3) In relation to a claim for universal credit made by a person other than the diagnosed or infected person referred to in paragraph (1)(a)(i), a payment received from the scheme or trust or which derives from a payment received from the scheme or trust, is to be disregarded if it would be disregarded in relation to an award of state pension credit by virtue of paragraph 13 or 15 of Schedule 5 to the State Pension Credit Regulations 2002.
@ref reg 76(2) and (3) (src:1244-1245)
GIVEN payment IS A `Payment considered under regulation 76`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 76 — the payment is disregarded in the calculation of capital or income` payment MEANS
        (`reg 76(2) — the payment is disregarded` payment)
    OR  (`reg 76(3) — the payment is disregarded for a claim by another person` payment)

-- Paragraph (4): definitions. "Miscarriage of justice compensation payment" means (a) a payment under section 133(1) of the Criminal
-- Justice Act 1988, or (b) any other payment by the Secretary of State, the Scottish Ministers or, in Northern Ireland, the Department
-- of Justice, to compensate a person for a miscarriage of justice in criminal proceedings or for being wrongfully charged with a
-- criminal offence. The other definitions ("the Horizon system", "the Post Office", "vaccine damage payment") are by citation of
-- documents that are not inputs, and are the facts of the fields above.
-- src:1248 | “miscarriage of justice compensation payment” means—
-- src:1249 | (a) a payment made under section 133(1) of the Criminal Justice Act 1988; or
-- src:1250 | (b) any other payment made by the Secretary of State, the Scottish Ministers or, in Northern Ireland, the Department of Justice, for the purpose of compensating a person—
-- src:1251 | (i) for a miscarriage of justice in criminal proceedings, or
-- src:1252 | (ii) for being wrongfully charged with a criminal offence;
@ref reg 76(4) (src:1248-1252)
DECLARE `Payment that may be a miscarriage of justice compensation payment` HAS
    `payment made under section 133(1) of the Criminal Justice Act 1988`                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `payment made by the Secretary of State, the Scottish Ministers or, in Northern Ireland, the Department of Justice`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `made for the purpose of compensating a person for a miscarriage of justice in criminal proceedings`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `made for the purpose of compensating a person for being wrongfully charged with a criminal offence`  IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:1248 | “miscarriage of justice compensation payment” means—
-- src:1249 | (a) a payment made under section 133(1) of the Criminal Justice Act 1988; or
-- src:1250 | (b) any other payment made by the Secretary of State, the Scottish Ministers or, in Northern Ireland, the Department of Justice, for the purpose of compensating a person—
-- src:1251 | (i) for a miscarriage of justice in criminal proceedings, or
-- src:1252 | (ii) for being wrongfully charged with a criminal offence;
@ref reg 76(4) (src:1248-1252)
GIVEN payment IS A `Payment that may be a miscarriage of justice compensation payment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 76(4) — miscarriage of justice compensation payment, limb (b)` payment MEANS
        (payment's `payment made by the Secretary of State, the Scottish Ministers or, in Northern Ireland, the Department of Justice`)
    AND (    (payment's `made for the purpose of compensating a person for a miscarriage of justice in criminal proceedings`)
          OR (payment's `made for the purpose of compensating a person for being wrongfully charged with a criminal offence`))

-- src:1248 | “miscarriage of justice compensation payment” means—
-- src:1249 | (a) a payment made under section 133(1) of the Criminal Justice Act 1988; or
-- src:1250 | (b) any other payment made by the Secretary of State, the Scottish Ministers or, in Northern Ireland, the Department of Justice, for the purpose of compensating a person—
-- src:1251 | (i) for a miscarriage of justice in criminal proceedings, or
-- src:1252 | (ii) for being wrongfully charged with a criminal offence;
@ref reg 76(4) (src:1248-1252)
GIVEN payment IS A `Payment that may be a miscarriage of justice compensation payment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 76(4) — miscarriage of justice compensation payment` payment MEANS
        (payment's `payment made under section 133(1) of the Criminal Justice Act 1988`)
    OR  (`reg 76(4) — miscarriage of justice compensation payment, limb (b)` payment)

§§ `Regulation 76(4) -- Other definitions (inert)`
-- src:1246 | (4) In this regulation—
-- src:1247 | “the Horizon system” means any version of the computer system used by the Post Office known as Horizon, Horizon Legacy, Horizon Online or HNG-X;
-- src:1253 | “the Post Office” means Post Office Limited (registered number 02154540);
-- src:1254 | “vaccine damage payment” means a payment made under the Vaccine Damage Payments Act 1979.
-- INERT as rules: "the Horizon system" (any version of the Post Office's computer system known as Horizon, Horizon Legacy, Horizon
-- Online or HNG-X), "the Post Office" (Post Office Limited, registered number 02154540) and "vaccine damage payment" (a payment under
-- the Vaccine Damage Payments Act 1979) name things by citation of documents that are not inputs; each is the fact of a field of
-- `Payment considered under regulation 76`.

§§ `Regulation 77 -- Company analogous to a partnership or one person business`

-- src:1255 | 77 Company analogous to a partnership or one person business
-- src:1256 | (1) Where a person stands in a position analogous to that of a sole owner or partner in relation to a company which is carrying on a trade or a property business, the person is to be treated, for the purposes of this Part, as the sole owner or partner.
-- src:1257 | (2) Where paragraph (1) applies, the person is to be treated, subject to paragraph (3)(a), as possessing an amount of capital equal to the value, or the person's share of the value, of the capital of the company and the value of the person's holding in the company is to be disregarded.
-- src:1258 | (3) Where paragraph (1) applies in relation to a company which is carrying on a trade—
-- src:1259 | (a) any assets of the company that are used wholly and exclusively for the purposes of the trade are to be disregarded from the person's capital while they are engaged in activities in the course of that trade;
-- src:1260 | (b) the income of the company or the person's share of that income is to be treated as the person's income and calculated in the manner set out in regulation 57 as if it were self-employed earnings; and
-- src:1261 | (c) where the person's activities in the course of the trade are their main employment, the person is to be treated as if they were in gainful self-employment and, accordingly, regulation 62 (minimum income floor) applies. ....
-- src:1262 | (4) Any self-employed earnings which the person is treated as having by virtue of paragraph (3)(b) are in addition to any employed earnings the person receives as a director or employee of the company.
-- src:1263 | (5) This regulation does not apply where the person derives income from the company that is employed earnings by virtue of Chapter 8 (workers under arrangements made by intermediaries), Chapter 9 (managed service companies) or Chapter 10 (workers’ services provided through intermediaries) of Part 2 of ITEPA and that income is derived from activities that are the person’s main employment.
-- src:1264 | (6) In paragraph (1) “property business” has the meaning in section 204 of the Corporation Tax Act 2009 .
@ref reg 77 (src:1255-1264)
DECLARE `Person in relation to a company` HAS
    `the person stands in a position analogous to that of a sole owner or partner in relation to the company`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the company is carrying on a trade`                                                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `the company is carrying on a property business`                                            IS A BOOLEAN
    `value of the capital of the company`                                                       IS A NUMBER
    `fraction of the value that is the person's share`                                          IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `value of any assets of the company that are used wholly and exclusively for the purposes of the trade`  IS A NUMBER
    `the person is engaged in activities in the course of that trade`                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person's activities in the course of the trade are their main employment`              IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person derives income from the company that is employed earnings by virtue of Chapter 8, 9 or 10 of Part 2 of ITEPA`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `that income is derived from activities that are the person's main employment`              IS A BOOLEAN
    `the self-employed earnings the person is treated as having by virtue of paragraph (3)(b)` IS A `Self-employed earnings considered under regulation 57`
    `employed earnings the person receives as a director or employee of the company`           IS A NUMBER

-- Paragraph (5): the regulation does not apply where the person derives income from the company that is employed earnings by virtue of
-- Chapter 8 (workers under arrangements made by intermediaries), Chapter 9 (managed service companies) or Chapter 10 (workers'
-- services provided through intermediaries) of Part 2 of ITEPA and that income is derived from activities that are the person's main
-- employment.
-- src:1263 | (5) This regulation does not apply where the person derives income from the company that is employed earnings by virtue of Chapter 8 (workers under arrangements made by intermediaries), Chapter 9 (managed service companies) or Chapter 10 (workers’ services provided through intermediaries) of Part 2 of ITEPA and that income is derived from activities that are the person’s main employment.
@ref reg 77(5) (src:1263)
GIVEN person IS A `Person in relation to a company`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 77(5) — this regulation does not apply` person MEANS
        (person's `the person derives income from the company that is employed earnings by virtue of Chapter 8, 9 or 10 of Part 2 of ITEPA`)
    AND (person's `that income is derived from activities that are the person's main employment`)

-- Paragraph (1): a person in a position analogous to that of a sole owner or partner in relation to a company carrying on a trade or
-- a property business is treated as the sole owner or partner, for the purposes of Part 6.
-- src:1256 | (1) Where a person stands in a position analogous to that of a sole owner or partner in relation to a company which is carrying on a trade or a property business, the person is to be treated, for the purposes of this Part, as the sole owner or partner.
@ref reg 77(1) (src:1256)
GIVEN person IS A `Person in relation to a company`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 77(1) — the person is treated as the sole owner or partner` person MEANS
        (person's `the person stands in a position analogous to that of a sole owner or partner in relation to the company`)
    AND (    (person's `the company is carrying on a trade`)
          OR (person's `the company is carrying on a property business`))
    AND (NOT (`reg 77(5) — this regulation does not apply` person))

-- Paragraph (3)(a): where the company carries on a trade, its assets used wholly and exclusively for the purposes of the trade are
-- disregarded from the person's capital while they are engaged in activities in the course of that trade.
-- src:1259 | (a) any assets of the company that are used wholly and exclusively for the purposes of the trade are to be disregarded from the person's capital while they are engaged in activities in the course of that trade;
@ref reg 77(3)(a) (src:1259)
GIVEN person IS A `Person in relation to a company`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 77(3)(a) — the value of the company's assets that are disregarded` person MEANS
    IF     (`reg 77(1) — the person is treated as the sole owner or partner` person)
       AND (person's `the company is carrying on a trade`)
       AND (person's `the person is engaged in activities in the course of that trade`)
    THEN person's `value of any assets of the company that are used wholly and exclusively for the purposes of the trade`
    ELSE 0

-- Paragraph (2): the person is treated as possessing capital equal to the value, or the person's share of the value, of the capital of
-- the company (subject to (3)(a)), and the value of the person's holding in the company is disregarded. The share is a fraction of the
-- whole; with none stated, the whole is the person's (sole owner).
-- src:1257 | (2) Where paragraph (1) applies, the person is to be treated, subject to paragraph (3)(a), as possessing an amount of capital equal to the value, or the person's share of the value, of the capital of the company and the value of the person's holding in the company is to be disregarded.
@ref reg 77(2) (src:1257)
GIVEN person IS A `Person in relation to a company`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 77(2) — the capital the person is treated as possessing` person MEANS
    IF `reg 77(1) — the person is treated as the sole owner or partner` person
    THEN `core — an amount rounded to the nearest penny`
            ((CONSIDER person's `fraction of the value that is the person's share`
              WHEN JUST share THEN share
              WHEN NOTHING THEN 1)
             TIMES (max 0 ((person's `value of the capital of the company`) MINUS (`reg 77(3)(a) — the value of the company's assets that are disregarded` person))))
    ELSE 0

-- src:1257 | (2) Where paragraph (1) applies, the person is to be treated, subject to paragraph (3)(a), as possessing an amount of capital equal to the value, or the person's share of the value, of the capital of the company and the value of the person's holding in the company is to be disregarded.
@ref reg 77(2) (src:1257)
GIVEN person IS A `Person in relation to a company`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 77(2) — the value of the person's holding in the company is disregarded` person MEANS
    `reg 77(1) — the person is treated as the sole owner or partner` person

-- Paragraph (3)(b): the income of the company, or the person's share of it, is treated as the person's income and calculated as
-- regulation 57 provides for self-employed earnings. The calculation is regulation 57(2); the caller supplies its inputs in the
-- field of the record.
-- src:1258 | (3) Where paragraph (1) applies in relation to a company which is carrying on a trade—
-- src:1259 | (a) any assets of the company that are used wholly and exclusively for the purposes of the trade are to be disregarded from the person's capital while they are engaged in activities in the course of that trade;
-- src:1260 | (b) the income of the company or the person's share of that income is to be treated as the person's income and calculated in the manner set out in regulation 57 as if it were self-employed earnings; and
@ref reg 77(3)(b) (src:1258-1260)
GIVEN person IS A `Person in relation to a company`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 77(3)(b) — the self-employed earnings the person is treated as having` person MEANS
    IF     (`reg 77(1) — the person is treated as the sole owner or partner` person)
       AND (person's `the company is carrying on a trade`)
    THEN `reg 57(2) — the self-employed earnings for an assessment period` (person's `the self-employed earnings the person is treated as having by virtue of paragraph (3)(b)`)
    ELSE 0

-- Paragraph (3)(c): where the person's activities in the course of the trade are their main employment, the person is treated as if
-- in gainful self-employment, and accordingly regulation 62 applies. The text after "applies." is a run of full stops.
-- src:1261 | (c) where the person's activities in the course of the trade are their main employment, the person is to be treated as if they were in gainful self-employment and, accordingly, regulation 62 (minimum income floor) applies. ....
@ref reg 77(3)(c) (src:1261)
GIVEN person IS A `Person in relation to a company`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 77(3)(c) — the person is treated as being in gainful self-employment` person MEANS
        (`reg 77(1) — the person is treated as the sole owner or partner` person)
    AND (person's `the company is carrying on a trade`)
    AND (person's `the person's activities in the course of the trade are their main employment`)

-- Paragraph (4): the self-employed earnings are in addition to any employed earnings the person receives as a director or employee.
-- src:1262 | (4) Any self-employed earnings which the person is treated as having by virtue of paragraph (3)(b) are in addition to any employed earnings the person receives as a director or employee of the company.
@ref reg 77(4) (src:1262)
GIVEN person IS A `Person in relation to a company`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 77(4) — the person's earned income from the company` person MEANS
    `core — an amount rounded to the nearest penny`
        ((`reg 77(3)(b) — the self-employed earnings the person is treated as having` person) PLUS (person's `employed earnings the person receives as a director or employee of the company`))

§§ `Regulation 77(6) -- Definition of "property business" (inert)`
-- src:1264 | (6) In paragraph (1) “property business” has the meaning in section 204 of the Corporation Tax Act 2009 .
-- INERT: defines "property business" by pure citation of section 204 of the Corporation Tax Act 2009, which is not an input. The
-- fact is the field `the company is carrying on a property business` of `Person in relation to a company`.
